course: dictionary
lesson: 5976
title: A word about a people and their past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mayan is a word you will meet in history and maths lessons. It describes things that belong to the Maya, the people of Central America, whose ancient civilisation built stone cities and pyramids. The clues help: «Millions of Maya people still live in the same lands today» tells you the Maya are a people, not a place.
explain: Look at the words next to Mayan. You will see «Mayan calendar», «Mayan pyramid», «Mayan numbers» and «Mayan gods». In each phrase, Mayan tells you where the thing comes from. Just as French describes things from France, Mayan describes things from the Maya.
explain: Maya is the name of the people, and Mayan describes what belongs to them, such as their languages. «Many Maya cities in the southern lowlands declined around 800 to 900, but millions of Maya people live today and speak around 30 Mayan languages.» So the Maya did not disappear, and their languages are still spoken.
fact: Mayan is an adjective when it describes things, such as «Mayan pyramid» or «Mayan calendar».
fact: Mayan means to do with the Maya, the people of Central America (Mexico, Guatemala, Belize and Honduras).
fact: A Maya person can also be called a Mayan, and millions of people still speak Mayan languages today.
fact: The ancient Maya built stone cities and pyramids, such as Chichén Itzá, and they used a writing system of glyphs, a calendar and zero.
fact: Mayan numbers use dots for 1, bars for 5 and a shell for zero, and they count in twenties.
exercise: «The ancient Maya built stone pyramids in Central America.» In the phrase «Mayan pyramid», what does Mayan tell you? | It is a type of very tall tree | It is to do with the Vikings | *It is to do with the Maya people | It is a kind of cold drink
exercise: A maths teacher writes «Mayan numbers use dots and bars.» Where do these numbers come from? | From the Olympic Games | From the numbers we use to count money | *From the Maya people of Central America | From the shops on the high street
exercise: «Millions of Maya people still live in the same lands today.» Find and copy one word that names a people. | still | millions | lands | *Maya
test: «Millions of Maya people still speak Mayan languages today.» In this sentence, what does Maya name? | *A people | A type of stone | A number | A language
test: Which country is NOT on the list of countries where the Maya lived? | *Canada | Honduras | Guatemala | Belize
exam: Jayden says Mayan only means a pyramid. What is the best reply? | *No, Mayan means to do with the Maya people | Yes, it always means a pyramid | No, it only means a kind of chocolate | Yes, it only means a calendar
